course: dictionary
lesson: 14889
title: Recollect: remember, gather, or calm down
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Recollect is a verb, so it is something you do. Its most common meaning is to remember something from the past, often when you have to think hard. «I don't recollect his name» means I tried to remember it, but I could not.
explain: It is a slightly formal word for remember. You might meet it in old stories, history books, or a witness's account of what happened. «As far as I can recollect, we left at noon» means I think we left at noon, but I am not completely sure.
explain: Watch for the hyphen. Re-collect, with a hyphen, means to collect or gather again: «Please re-collect the worksheets.» A third, formal meaning is to calm yourself: «She paused to recollect herself» means she stopped to calm down and get her thoughts together. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Recollect means to remember something from the past, often with effort.
fact: Re-collect, with a hyphen, means to collect or gather again.
fact: «Recollect oneself» means to calm down and get your thoughts together.
fact: Recollect is a little more formal than remember, so you will often see it in stories, memoirs and history books.
exercise: «I don't recollect his name.» What does recollect mean here? | *To remember something from the past | To calm yourself down | To gather things together again | To forget it completely
exercise: «Please re-collect the worksheets from the desks.» What does re-collect mean? | To throw the worksheets away | To draw pictures on the worksheets | To lose them forever | *To collect them again
exercise: «She paused to recollect herself after the shock.» What does recollect herself mean? | To go to sleep | *To calm down and get her thoughts together | To run out of the room | To forget her own name
test: «As far as I can recollect, the shop closes at five.» What does the phrase «as far as I can recollect» show? | The shop is already closed | *The speaker is remembering, but may not be completely sure | The speaker is angry about the shop | The speaker knows for certain
test: «The old soldier began to recollect the battle, step by step.» What is he doing? | Gathering the soldiers together again | Running away from the battle | Buying a new coat | *Remembering the events of the past
exam: Which sentence uses recollect to mean calm yourself? | I can't recollect where I left my bag | *She stopped and tried to recollect herself before she spoke | He will recollect the team in the morning | Please recollect the spare pencils from the box
